<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">John Ernest IV, Duke of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1658">1658</a>–<a href="/years/1729">1729</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">John Ernest IV, Duke of Saxe-Coburg-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saalfeld">Saalfeld</a>, was the seventh son of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ernest-i-duke-of-saxe-gotha">Ernest the Pious</a> of Saxe-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gotha">Gotha</a>. He received Saalfeld in 1680, and after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/duchy-of-saxe-coburg">Duchy of Saxe-Coburg</a> died out in 1699 he gained much of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coburg">Coburg</a>, founding the line of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld. His descendants later married into many royal houses of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/europe">Europe</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/john-ernest-iv-duke-of-saxe-coburg-saalfeld.jpg" alt="John Ernest IV, Duke of Saxe-Coburg-Saalfeld" width="320" height="492" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Wolfgang Philipp Kilian · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Arolsen_Klebeband_01_177_2.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
